[Event "Hoogovens Tournament"]
[Site "Wijk aan Zee, Netherlands"]
[Date "1999.01.20"]
[Round "4"]
[White "Garry Kasparov"]
[Black "Veselin Topalov"]
[Result "1-0"]
[Id "sample-kasparov-topalov-1999"]
[Title "Kasparov vs Topalov, 1999 - Kasparov's Immortal"]
[Kind "sample"]

1. e4 {I claim the centre with my king's pawn.} d6 {A flexible setup. I will put my bishop on g7 later.}
2. d4 Nf6 3. Nc3 g6 4. Be3 Bg7 5. Qd2 {Queen and bishop line up to swap off Black's best bishop.} c6
6. f3 b5 7. Nge2 Nbd7 8. Bh6 {Offer to trade bishops so Black's king loses its guard.} Bxh6
9. Qxh6 Bb7 10. a3 e5 11. O-O-O {I castle queenside and get my king to safety.} Qe7
12. Kb1 a6 13. Nc1 O-O-O {I castle queenside too. Both kings are now on the same side.}
14. Nb3 exd4 15. Rxd4 c5 16. Rd1 Nb6 17. g3 Kb8 18. Na5 Ba8 19. Bh3 d5
20. Qf4+ {Check! Black's king has to step into the corner.} Ka7 21. Rhe1 d4 22. Nd5 Nbxd5
23. exd5 Qd6 24. Rxd4 {A rook sacrifice! If Black takes it, the king gets dragged into the open.}
cxd4 {I'll take the free rook and see if the attack really works.}
25. Re7+ {Check. The black king has nowhere safe to hide.} Kb6 26. Qxd4+ Kxa5
27. b4+ {Another check, pulling the king even further up the board.} Ka4 28. Qc3 Qxd5
29. Ra7 Bb7 30. Rxb7 Qc4 31. Qxf6 {I win a knight while the king is stuck on my side of the board.} Kxa3
32. Qxa6+ Kxb4 33. c3+ Kxc3 34. Qa1+ Kd2 35. Qb2+ Kd1
36. Bf1 {A quiet move with a sharp idea: my bishop now attacks Black's queen.} Rd2 37. Rd7 Rxd7
38. Bxc4 bxc4 39. Qxh8 Rd3 40. Qa8 c3 41. Qa4+ Ke1 42. f4 f5 43. Kc1 Rd2
44. Qa7 {Black can no longer stop my passed pawns and threats. Black resigns.} 1-0
